// session-verbs.storyarc
// part of Arcturus, a programming language and compiler for the Infocom Z-machine.
// Copyright (c) 2026, Stefan Vogt.
// https://github.com/ByteProject/Arcturus
//
// A showcase for the session verbs (docs/01 Part I section 10): VERSION prints
// the banner mid-game and is ALWAYS in, the bug-reporter's friend.
// NOTIFY brings the classic score bracket line: off by default, enabled
// here in `on start`, toggleable by the player, and the two are coupled,
// enabling the feature anywhere brings the verb along, while a game that
// never touches `notify` has no lines, no verb, and not even the
// dictionary word. And the oldest Easter egg in the medium answers: a
// player who curses gets a dry line back, an extendedverbs family
// selected as `swear`. Compile and run:
//
//   arcc examples/features/session-verbs.storyarc -o session.z5
//   frotz session.z5
//
// Try, in order:
//   version              the banner, mid-game: which build is this?
//   take medal           "[Your score has just gone up by 5.]": notify
//                        was enabled in on start
//   notify               the player turns the bracket lines off
//   drop medal           silence (the score still moves; SCORE shows it)
//   take medal           still silent
//   notify               back on
//   damn                 the Easter egg answers, dryly

game
    title  "The Trophy Room"
    headline "A session-verbs showcase"
    author "Stefan Vogt"
    start  trophyroom
    scoring

summon.statusline
summon.extendedverbs swear

on start
    change notify to true

room trophyroom
    name "The Trophy Room"
    desc "Velvet, glass, and one medal nobody dusted."

thing medal in trophyroom
    name "tin medal"
    words medal, tin
    scored
    desc "Third place, unspecified discipline, deeply loved once."
